# ddraw.dll exports: Wine's 32-bit ddraw.dll plus the extra ones in Windows' ddraw.dll. DirectDrawCreate and
# DirectDrawCreateEx are implemented by the core (they load the mods first); the rest jump to the system ddraw.dll.
# Each line: the export name and its stdcall argument bytes (from the DDK headers; InternalLock/InternalUnlock are
# undocumented and follow DDInternalLock/Unlock). The size matters only for an export the system ddraw.dll lacks:
# its stand-in returns E_NOTIMPL and pops exactly that many bytes, so a caller's stack stays intact.
AcquireDDThreadLock 0
CompleteCreateSysmemSurface 4
D3DParseUnknownCommand 8
DDGetAttachedSurfaceLcl 12
DDHAL32_VidMemAlloc 16
DDHAL32_VidMemFree 12
DDInternalLock 8
DDInternalUnlock 4
DirectDrawCreate 12
DirectDrawCreateClipper 12
DirectDrawCreateEx 16
DirectDrawEnumerateA 8
DirectDrawEnumerateExA 12
DirectDrawEnumerateExW 12
DirectDrawEnumerateW 8
DllCanUnloadNow 0
DllGetClassObject 12
DllRegisterServer 0
DllUnregisterServer 0
DSoundHelp 12
GetDDSurfaceLocal 12
GetNextMipMap 4
GetOLEThunkData 4
GetSurfaceFromDC 12
HeapVidMemAllocAligned 20
InternalLock 8
InternalUnlock 4
LateAllocateSurfaceMem 16
RegisterSpecialCase 16
ReleaseDDThreadLock 0
SetAppCompatData 8
VidMemAlloc 12
VidMemAmountFree 4
VidMemFini 4
VidMemFree 8
VidMemInit 20
VidMemLargestFree 4
